      "writtenOn": "2023-05-04T09:10:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if we deprecate `BATTERY_LEVEL_NEAR_FULL` and change it to `charge_get_display_charge() \u003c 1000`, there will be a gap between [BATTERY_LEVEL_NEAR_FULL](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/battery.h;l\u003d32;drc\u003df0436fe4c66f1a6759c2ae28157ec495b53eab9c) and [PWR_STATE_CHARGE_NEAR_FULL](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/charge_state_v2.c;l\u003d2273;drc\u003d03cad4ad498b96cb9084e039fbc7ab30cc919b6c), there are many boards defined LED behavior that depends on `BATTERY_LEVEL_NEAR_FULL` and `PWR_STATE_CHARGE_NEAR_FULL`, such as [voltorb](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/corsola/voltorb/project.overlay;l\u003d88;drc\u003da10cb8394d26d9c369eb5bd1c2ab64f0e955a898), so the LED behavior between `BATTERY_LEVEL_NEAR_FULL` and `PWR_STATE_CHARGE_NEAR_FULL` will become undefined.",
